  "prefLabel": "Env-A 1203.59 Open molding",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 1203.59 “Open molding” means a family of techniques for composite fabrication which makes use of single-cavity molds and requires little or no external pressure.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-A 1200) #9933, eff 6-1-11; ss by #12899, eff 10-17-19",
